, managing the recruiting database, and meeting all NCAA compliance regulations. This position will plan and coordinate all team travel within available resources. The pos... View Details Bookmark Systems Administrator 08/21/2026 Staff - Exempt (Monthly) Systems Administration Reporting to the Director of Systems Administration, the Systems Administrator assists the team in maintaining, upgrading and securing multiple data centers between on-prem and cloud services, to support enterprise computing, storage, data integrity and backup infrastructure and services.Deploy, support and maintain Windows, Linux and Unix virtual and physical environments.Patch and maintain th... View Details Bookmark Senior Associate Athletic Director/Chief Revenue Officer 08/20/2026 Staff - Exempt (Monthly) Athletics Internal Operations The Senior Associate Athletic Director/Chief Revenue Officer serves as a senior leader responsible for advancing revenue generation, philanthropic development, commercial strategy, customer engagement, and business innovation for Murray State Athletics. Reporting directly to the Assistant Vice president & Deputy Director of Athletics/COO, the Chief Revenue Officer combines strategic thinkin... View Details Bookmark Director of Expo Center 08/19/2026 Staff - Exempt (Monthly) West KY Expo Ctr The Expo Director is responsible for the successful operation of the Cherry West Kentucky Livestock and Exposition (Expo) Center, a 2,748 seat multi-event building.Serve as the primary liaison between building users and University staff.Prepare and direct the preparation of marketing/promotional campaigns designed to enhance the facilities’ reputation and maximize usage, as well as making prese... View Details Bookmark Assistant Vice President for Facilities Management 08/06/2026 Staff - Exempt (Monthly) VP for Finance and Admin Services Responsible for assisting the Vice President for Finance and Administrative Services (VPFAS) in managing the daily operations and strategic planning of the university facilities. Includes responsibility for all aspects of facility project development and management, as well as direct supervision over the directors and associate directors of Building and Equipment Maintenance, Environmental Safe... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor, Physiology 08/04/2026 10/02/2026 Faculty (Tenure-Track) Biological Sciences The primary teaching responsibilities will be upper level Animal Physiology, which is taken by Pre-Medical, Pre-Dental, and Pre-Optometry majors who are close to applying for professional school. The candidate will also teach Human Physiology, as well as some introductory biology courses. There will be opportunities to teach other upper level courses and graduate level courses in the successful... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor, Cell Biology 08/04/2026 10/02/2026 Faculty (Tenure-Track) Biological Sciences The primary teaching responsibilities will be introductory level Cell Biology, upper-level Cell Biology, and an upper-level course in the candidate’s area of expertise. The research area may be in any field of cellular and molecular biology. The successful candidate will conduct research and publish their work, pursue external funding, mentor undergraduate and graduate student research, and adv... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor, Economics 07/28/2026 Faculty (Tenure-Track) Economics and Finance Applicants in all fields of economics will be considered. The successful candidate must demonstrate a commitment to excellent teaching as well as a promising research agenda. The typical course load would be three courses per semester and may include web instruction. View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor, Organic Chemistry 07/21/2026 10/15/2026 Faculty (Tenure-Track) Chemistry The Department of Chemistry invites applications from individuals committed to being excellent teacher-scholars at a primarily undergraduate institution. The successful candidate will be expected to teach a 3/2 course load including foundational organic chemistry courses, teaching laboratory courses, and advanced courses in their sub-discipline to both undergraduate and graduate (Masters) stude... View Details Bookmark Veterinary Pathologist/Assistant Professor 07/15/2026 Faculty (Non-Tenure-Track) Breathitt Veterinary Center Murray State University is seeking a full-time Veterinary Pathologist/Assistant Professor for its Hopkinsville, KY location.The Veterinary Pathologist/Assistant Professor’s primary responsibilities include the following:Perform necropsies on animal carcasses and report appropriate findings.Interpret histopathology slides of necropsy submissions and report findings.Conduct appropriate research a... View Details Bookmark Veterinary Diagnostician/Assistant Professor 07/15/2026 Faculty (Non-Tenure-Track) Breathitt Veterinary Center Serves as liaison between the laboratory and customers, receiving diagnostic samples, routing for testing, serving as a case coordinator, releasing test results, and answering customer and staff questions.Liaison with referring veterinarians, owners, staff, food producers, government agencies, and other laboratories.Receives diagnostic samples for testing (e.g., takes case history, unloads anim... View Details Bookmark Instructor/Assistant Professor, Criminal Justice 07/15/2026 Faculty (Tenure-Track) Criminal Justice and Social Work This position will have a teaching load of 12 credit hours per semester. As this is a small undergraduate program, the ability to teach a variety of courses across the criminal justice curriculum is expected. The successful applicant will also be expected to teach graduate level criminal justice courses in the online CRJ concentration of the new MSU MBA program.Responsibilities:Teach a variety ... View Details Bookmark Compensation Analyst 05/29/2026 Staff - Exempt (Monthly) Human Resources The Compensation Analyst supports the design, implementation, and administration of compensation programs and projects within the University. This role assists with salary benchmarking, job audits, position placement, and compensation data analysis to ensure competitive and equitable pay practices aligned with organizational policies and market trends. This role is responsible for completing sa... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor, Counseling 06/10/2026 Faculty (Tenure-Track) Ed Studies Ldrshp Cnslng The successful candidate will (1) teach a minimum of three courses per semester; (2) coordinate counseling operations for the Counseling and Assessment Center, as needed; (3) maintain an advising caseload of graduate and undergraduate students; (4) supervise practicum and internship students; (5) engage in professional research and scholarly activities; (6) pursue involvement in appropriate pro... View Details Bookmark Assistant/Associate Professor, Accounting 06/11/2026 Faculty (Tenure-Track) Accounting Principal responsibility for candidates with be teaching accounting courses at the undergraduate and graduate level. Engagement in research resulting in publications in recognized refereed journals and providing university and regional service are also required. View Details Bookmark 412 Sparks Hall Murray, KY 42071 - msu.hr@murraystate.edu - (270) 809-2146 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
