      "title": "Murray State University: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:www.murraystatejobs.com,2005:/postings/all_jobs Murray State University: All Jobs 2026-09-04T13:30:46-05:00 https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12857 2026-09-04T13:30:45-05:00 2026-09-04T13:30:46-05:00 Senior Accountant, Reporting and Tax <div>Assist in preparation of quarterly and annual financial statements and audits, completion of audit workpapers, general ledger reconciliation, and ad hoc analysis. Conduct advanced research on tax laws and regulations, and analyze complex tax issues and determine appropriate treatment. Develop and implement procedures and coordinate tax compliance with functional areas within Accounting and Financial Services.<br><br></div><ul><li>Assist with monthly closing of accounting records and related reporting as well as year-end financial statement processing, including the annual audit.</li><li>Responsible for key reconciliations, financial reports and audit functions to ensure deadlines are met (such as sales tax, UBIT, general audit).</li><li>Perform analytical procedures, including investigation of unusual transactions or unexpected variances, on monthly financial reports.</li><li>Handle departmental reconciliations that need clear segregation of duties to perform.</li><li>Provide support for the development and documentation of departmental policies and procedures.</li><li>Provide support to Assistant Director and department with reporting responsibilities and debt management.</li><li>Provide daily monitoring and review of cash transactions and bank account reconciliations.</li><li>Interpret GAAP, GASB and FASB guidance and maintain working knowledge to ensure proper reporting of financial data.</li><li>Analyze department sales for unrelated business income tax purposes and annual supporting documentation for UBIT.</li><li>Research and interpret tax regulations and compliance impacting University Operations.</li><li>Prepare documentation and support schedules related to institutional tax reporting and compliance requirements.</li><li>Monitor regulatory changes and communicate impacts to departmental leadership.</li><li>Develop, document, and maintain accounting and tax procedures and internal controls, and recommend process improvements to strengthen compliance, reporting and accuracy and operational efficiency.</li><li>Stay informed of changes in tax compliance, monitor accounting and tax guidance and be a resource to other areas of accounting and financial services.</li><li>Other duties as assigned.</li></ul> Accounting and Financial Services https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12841 2026-08-28T08:34:01-05:00 2026-08-28T08:34:02-05:00 Administrative Specialist <div>Administrative support and data maintenance. Provides essential services to TES regarding processing undergraduate and graduate student's information and documents in relation to certifications, endorsements, and rank changes through approved programs.<br><br></div><ul><li>Enter accurate records of admission and exit information for undergraduate and graduate students who are participating in EPSB approved educator preparation programs.</li><li>Review the yearly Admission &amp; Exit report for accuracy and completeness before submitting to the state.</li><li>Verify students have met coursework and assessment requirements prior to issuing a recommendation to the state for the student's certification, endorsement, or rank change.</li><li>Maintain a complete record of recommendations, denials, and additional information for each student enrolled in an approved program and use these records to pull reports together as needed for TES.</li><li>Generate early notification letters for undergraduate students who are pending graduation and have successfully completed the student teaching program.</li><li>Review weekly PRAXIS score reports sent to the University on behalf of students to denote which undergraduate and graduate students have met the assessment requirements for the program.</li><li>Assist the Director of TES as needed to gather information, pull records, and generate reports.</li><li>Collaborate with coworkers to update and maintain a digital database central to the success of TES.</li><li>Other duties as assigned.</li></ul> Teacher Education Services https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12815 2026-08-06T12:36:19-05:00 2026-08-06T12:36:20-05:00 Assistant Vice President for Facilities Management <div>Responsible for assisting the Vice President for Finance and Administrative Services (VPFAS) in managing the daily operations and strategic planning of the university facilities. Includes responsibility for all aspects of facility project development and management, as well as direct supervision over the directors and associate directors of Building and Equipment Maintenance, Environmental Safety &amp; Health, Facilities Finance and Administration, Grounds Maintenance and Building Services, Facilities Design &amp; Construction and third-party contracts for grounds and building services. The AVPFM assists in the development and implementation of campus sustainability initiatives, particularly as they relate to energy efficiency and the sustainable design and construction of campus facilities. Responsible for coordinating effective communication and collaboration between campus constituents and project architects, engineers, and the general contractor as well as making frequent presentations to legislative committees and the Board of Regents as required.<br><br></div><div>As head of the University’s Department for Facilities Management, the AVP provides general management, supervision, and professional direction to a comprehensive facilities management organization that provides facilities planning; space administration; architectural and engineering; construction management, facilities maintenance and repair; renovations; utilities generation and distribution; custodial; grounds landscape; recycling; and other maintenance services to the main campus, including Auxiliary Enterprises, the remote facilities of the Breathitt Veterinary Center (veterinary diagnostic center), Regional campus sites in Hopkinsville and Paducah, and Hancock Biological Station.<br><br></div><ul><li>Manages the overall department comprised of a workforce of approximately 65 employees</li><li>Responsible for an annual budget of approximately $13.5 million and manages an annual renovation volume of $10M (~200+ projects) and major design and construction projects of sometimes near $100 million dollars.</li><li>Manages contracts for third parties, primarily for custodial and grounds services.</li><li>Oversees Environmental Safety and Health to ensure adherence to applicable safety rules and health standards, as well as local, state and federal regulations.</li><li>Develops and recommends policies, planning guidelines, and procedures for the development of the University’s biennial capital budget program, and manages the program throughout the process of development, approval and implementation.</li><li>Develops and implements, or recommends, University policies and procedures for facilities and utilities systems management, maintenance, operation, and capital construction.</li><li>Maintains campus master plan and current boundary line information.</li><li>Maintains land and building data for campus facilities.</li><li>Responsible for compliance with all federal, state and local building codes and requirements.</li><li>Other duties as assigned.</li></ul> VP for Finance and Admin Services https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12739 2026-07-15T16:09:27-05:00 2026-07-15T16:09:27-05:00 Veterinary Pathologist/Assistant Professor <div>Murray State University is seeking a full-time Veterinary Pathologist/Assistant Professor for its Hopkinsville, KY location.<br><br></div><div>The Veterinary Pathologist/Assistant Professor’s primary responsibilities include the following:</div><ul><li>Perform necropsies on animal carcasses and report appropriate findings.</li><li>Interpret histopathology slides of necropsy submissions and report findings.</li><li>Conduct appropriate research and publish findings.</li><li>Provide consultations with veterinarians and livestock farmers.</li><li>Provide instruction, as required, for the Animal Health Technology curriculum.</li><li>Comply with Quality Management System.</li><li>Perform special projects as determined by Head of Pathology.</li></ul> Breathitt Veterinary Center https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12637 2026-06-11T10:40:16-05:00 2026-06-11T10:40:17-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor, Accounting <div>Principal responsibility for candidates with be teaching accounting courses at the undergraduate and graduate level. Engagement in research resulting in publications in recognized refereed journals and providing university and regional service are also required.</div> Accounting https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12851 2026-09-03T09:49:30-05:00 2026-09-03T09:49:31-05:00 BVC Business Coordinator <div>Performs administrative support, customer service, research, database management, strategic and budget planning, data analytics, and critical quality control documentation to ensure timely and accurate diagnostic reporting for nationally accredited Level 1 National Animal Health Network laboratory.<br><br></div><ul><li>Initiate diagnostic testing process by creating work process in Laboratory Information Management System.</li><li>Maintain accurate and detailed customer/vendor account information.</li><li>Exercise judgement (e.g. determining appropriate vendors, evaluating vendor performance, providing vendor feedback, addressing supply and logistical issues, etc.), to perform administrative functions required to purchase/order/process for payment critical supplies and equipment.</li><li>Interact with vendor, maintain building security, and ensure visitor compliance with laboratory quality and safety requirements.</li><li>Assist with grant budget and management</li><li>Plan/Coordinate internal/external administrative efforts. Create, maintain, and update administrative work processes. Monitor organizational budget and prepare informational reports. Develop budget reports for spending and revenue analysis</li><li>Interact with vendors and work with procurement to ensure purchasing compliance.</li><li>Research equipment and supplies for laboratory use</li><li>Coordinate with other laboratories for administrative and financial processes.</li><li>Prepare/distribute billing documents and process payments. Review invoices, prepare and approve payments. Reconcile accounting reports with expense and revenues</li><li>Maintain customer/personnel confidentiality</li><li>Complete required administrative and financial processes/reports/documents/ deposits etc.</li><li>Document process deficiencies and participate in developing resolution</li><li>Special projects as required</li><li>Liaison with HR and prepare personnel administrative documents</li><li>Exercise discretion and independent judgment with daily customer interactions to ensure complete and accurate data, fees charged, and fees charged, and customer inquiries.</li><li>Ensure compliance with critical quality/accreditation standards. Document control for admin work processes (ensure changes are properly documented, approved, implemented, and retained), accurate data input, documenting changes, obtaining appropriate approval for corrections. Creating a paper trail accreditation team to see a start to finish project with all changes properly approved/documented.</li><li>Complete national accreditation, university, and laboratory required training. In addition to University training, Lab Safety training, Periodic quality training, recognizing hazards, proper reporting of hazards, etc. Review new/changed administrative work processes and document the review was completed.</li><li>Maintain proficiency, skills, and knowledge to ensure compliance with laboratory quality/capacity requirements necessary to maintain a Level 1 laboratory status. Maintain database knowledge, data entry speed and accuracy, and familiarity with documents submitted to meet Level 1 advertised testing capabilities (e.g. 700-800 tests per day), quality reporting, message automation to nation agencies, and confidentiality.</li><li>Participate in quality process to include internal audits and national accreditation processes. Verifying data entry accuracy, logging customer complaints and additional customer instructions, creating a clear administrative trail (initial paperwork to final report to billing) for accreditation team members to review during the national visits. Investigate (determine root cause), document, develop corrective actions (how to avoid/minimize incomplete or inaccurate data), and implement corrective actions to eliminate or minimize future issues. Participate in periodic internal audits and non-conformance root cause working groups of work areas (to include other work areas) to ensure compliance with accreditation standards and documentation requirements. Participate in the nation accreditation by answering accreditation team questions (written and verbal), providing documentation showing work processes are followed and they are following internal and external processes. Continually review work area processes used for reliability and proper operation. They must be familiar with submitting problems, participating in developing solutions, and implementing resolution. Must address and clearly document data entry errors (e.g. corrected data, date change made, approval, etc.) and test request changes.&nbsp;</li><li>Other duties as assigned.</li></ul> Breathitt Veterinary Center https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12834 2026-08-20T13:47:00-05:00 2026-08-20T13:47:01-05:00 Senior Associate Athletic Director/Chief Revenue Officer <div>The Senior Associate Athletic Director/Chief Revenue Officer serves as a senior leader responsible for advancing revenue generation, philanthropic development, commercial strategy, customer engagement, and business innovation for Murray State Athletics. Reporting directly to the Assistant Vice president &amp; Deputy Director of Athletics/COO, the Chief Revenue Officer combines strategic thinking with hands-on operational leadership to build scalable revenue systems, optimize institutional assets, strengthen customer and constituent experiences, and position Murray State Athletics for sustainable commercial growth.<br><br></div><ul><li>Lead strategic and operational initiatives spanning ticket sales and service, premium seating, fundraising, membership enhancement, donor engagement, hospitality, customer relationship management, business intelligence, audience monetization, venue utilization, special events, parking and tailgating programs, licensing opportunities, and emerging business ventures.</li><li>Provide leadership and supervision for assigned revenue-generation and commercial-strategy personnel.</li><li>Develop and execute an integrated revenue-generation and commercial strategy aligned with the long-term vision, financial sustainability, and competitive ambitions of Murray State Athletics.</li><li>Lead ticketing strategy and operations across sales, service, retention, pricing, packaging, inventory management, reporting, and customer experience.</li><li>Develop strategies that grow attendance, improve customer acquisition and retention, strengthen fan loyalty, and increase the long-term value of customer relationships.</li><li>Develop integrated customer and constituent engagement strategies that strength lifelong relationships with fans, members, donors, partners, and the broader Murray State community.</li><li>Lead the development, positioning, sales strategy, and performance optimization of premium seating, hospitality products, and other enhanced customer experiences.</li><li>Develop and execute fundraising strategies that increase philanthropic support while aligning donor engagement initiatives with the long-term priorities of Murray State Athletics.</li><li>Cultivate meaningful relationships with major gift prospects, donors, alumni, and key stakeholders while supporting a culture of philanthropy throughout the department.</li><li>Lead membership enhancement initiatives designed to increase participation, strengthen donor acquisition and retention, and expand annual philanthropic support.</li><li>Oversee donor stewardship, donor services, and constituent engagement practices that deliver exceptional experiences and strengthen long-term donor relationships.</li><li>Build and oversee customer and constituent relationship management, business intelligence, forecasting, reporting, and revenue-performance systems that strengthen accountability and support informed decision-making.</li><li>Use pricing strategy, market research, audience segmentation, customer insights, and consumer-behavior data to identify growth opportunities and improve commercial performance.</li><li>Evaluate athletics facilities, events, programs, experiences, and other institutional assets to identify opportunities for increased utilization, monetization, and enterprise value.</li><li>Develop and advance special events, external rentals, hospitality programs, parking and tailgating initiatives, licensing opportunities, and other year-round commercial activities.</li><li>Identify, evaluate and develop new business ventures and nontraditional revenue opportunities consistent with university priorities and the Murray State Athletics brand.</li><li>Collaborate closely with the corporate sponsorship team to maximize partner value, identify integrated commercial opportunities, and align sponsorship assets with broader revenue and fan-engagement strategies.</li><li>Collaborate with the Brand, Communications &amp; Fan Engagement unit to align audience growth, campaign priorities, customer acquisition, game-day experiences, and year-round engagement efforts.</li><li>Partner with athletics leadership, University Advancement, event operations, facilities, finance, development, campus stakeholders, and external partners to ensure coordinated planning and execution across revenue-generating initiatives.</li><li>Recruit, lead, mentor, and develop assigned staff while establishing clear goals, performance standards, accountability measures, and professional-development opportunities.</li><li>Monitor trends across collegiate athletics, professional sports, entertainment, hospitality, technology, and consumer engagement to identify emerging opportunities and competitive advantages.</li><li>Manage assigned budgets, contracts, vendors, operational plans, and departmental resources in accordance with university policies and applicable legal, conference, and NCAA requirements.</li><li>Review, monitor and manage athletics accounts to ensure accuracy, timely processing, compliance with university, state and NCAA policies, and resolve account issues appropriately.</li><li>Other duties as assigned.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>As a member of the Murray State University Athletic Department, you shall comply with all applicable NCAA rules and regulations as provided in the NCAA Division I Manual. If you are found in violation of NCAA regulations, you shall be subject to disciplinary or corrective action as set forth in the provisions of the NCAA enforcement procedures, including suspension without pay or termination of employment for significant or repetitive violations.</div> Athletics Internal Operations https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12793 2026-07-28T14:43:42-05:00 2026-07-28T14:43:43-05:00 Assistant Professor, Economics <div>Applicants in all fields of economics will be considered. The successful candidate must demonstrate a commitment to excellent teaching as well as a promising research agenda. The typical course load would be three courses per semester and may include web instruction.</div> Economics and Finance https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12704 2026-07-08T10:49:14-05:00 2026-07-08T10:49:15-05:00 Compensation Analyst <div>The Compensation Analyst supports the design, implementation, and administration of compensation programs and projects within the University. This role assists with salary benchmarking, job audits, position placement, and compensation data analysis to ensure competitive and equitable pay practices aligned with organizational policies and market trends. This role is responsible for completing salary surveys, ensuring the integrity of compensation data, documenting processes and protocols, and serving as a key project member on compensation projects.<br><br></div><ul><li>Conduct Human Resource analytics, data analysis and interpretation of trends to support proactive planning related to faculty and staff compensation.</li><li>Analyze data and relevant market trends, assist with the regular review of established faculty pay plans and staff grade structures, and provide market analysis and recommendations.</li><li>Work closely with the Director of Human Resources and the Associate Director of Human Resources regarding the development, implementation and administration of compensation programs.</li><li>Responsible for completing annual institutional CUPA HR employment and compensation surveys, and other related compensation surveys on the University’s behalf.</li><li>Analyze data from survey sources to determine competitiveness both internally and externally.</li><li>Examine job audit questionnaires in order to determine proper classification, FLSA exempt/non-exempt status, staff grade, as well as to ensure consistency of position classification and compensation for all positions across campus.</li><li>Enhance knowledge of market relativity through wage surveys, job pricing and benchmarking, market analysis and analyzing internal data.</li><li>Analyze data and assist with presentation to stakeholders.</li><li>Ensure compliance with University policies and procedures, as well as all applicable federal and state wage regulations.</li><li>Assist the Associate Director of Human Resources and the Director of Human Resources in administering and communicating the compensation strategy and philosophy to administrators, faculty and staff across campus.</li><li>Responsible for developing the biennial salary roster for Board of Regents approval, including monitoring and reporting any compensation paid for faculty and staff that is in addition to the regular budgeted salary.</li><li>Respond to inquiries related to compensation policies and procedures.</li><li>Maintain confidentiality of sensitive employee compensation information.</li><li>Other duties as assigned.</li></ul> Human Resources https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12856 2026-09-04T09:24:39-05:00 2026-09-04T09:24:40-05:00 Accounting Specialist <div>Routine fiscal tasks of restricted funds, including grant and cost sharing reconciliations, and agency invoicing and reporting as well as office administrative and accounting duties.</div><div><br></div><ul><li>Specific Job Duties:<ul><li>Review month e-print reports to ensure documentation is complete and accurate for permanent grant file</li><li>Prepare and send final invoices to agencies</li><li>Reconcile and initiate closing of grants once final payment is received</li><li>Index grant documents in BDMS</li><li>Process receivables</li><li>Prepare and send monthly BVC invoices</li><li>Annual subcontract monitoring</li><li>Supervise student workers</li></ul></li><li>Office Administrative duties include:<ul><li>Coordinate ordering office supplies</li><li>Maintain office purchasing card</li></ul></li><li>Office Accounting duties include:<ul><li>Reconcile and mail checks</li><li>Petty Cash</li></ul></li><li>Perform other duties as requested by supervisory personnel</li></ul> Accounting and Financial Services https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12837 2026-08-21T11:25:28-05:00 2026-08-21T11:25:29-05:00 Director of Basketball Operations <div>The Director of Basketball Operations will direct the daily operations of the basketball program. The position will oversee all aspects of recruiting within the sport. This includes planning, and coordinating recruiting visits, managing the recruiting database, and meeting all NCAA compliance regulations. This position will plan and coordinate all team travel within available resources. The position will be responsible for scheduling contests to meet revenue obligations while maintaining competitive balance. The position will also be responsible for coordinating community relations and creating volunteer opportunities for student-athletes. Position will serve as the director for summer camps and clinics. Individual will be the lead contact for all operations of the sport program and direct liaison to the Head Coach.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities &amp; Duties</strong></div><div><strong>Recruiting:</strong></div><ul><li>Official and Unofficial Visits:<ul><li>Organize official and unofficial visits for recruits; Organize and coordinate recruit game-day logistics; coordinate meals, activities, seating, etc. for recruits during visits. Coordinating on campus visits and events, which includes:<ul><li>Official Visits: coordinate all hotel and travel accommodations for the prospective student athlete, Meetings with: professors on campus, athletic director, coaching staff, student-athlete and academic services, create schedules for each prospective student athlete along with itineraries for the visit, Coordinates all events throughout the visit.</li><li>Unofficial Visits: Coordinate prospective student-athletes schedule with coaches' schedule, schedule meetings with coaching staff, send out invitations to all home games, gather information about prospective student-athlete, give tour of campus and facilities, etc.</li></ul></li><li>Coordinating logistics for events, which includes: paperwork, compliance, itineraries, meetings, lodging, transportation, food, location, etc.</li></ul></li><li>Responsible for initiating the \"who and when\" of recruiting efforts: present prospect/team to coaching staff, strategically determine assistant coaches' travel destinations, providing list to compliance office of top prospects to visit, organizing head coaches' travel schedule, maintaining master recruiting schedule and calendar, distributing travel dates and locations to compliance &amp; business office personnel, provide assistant coaches with high school profile sheets, provide assistant coaches with recruiting materials for the road.</li><li>Maintaining the prospective student-athlete pool: Establish data bank of prospects utilizing varied recruiting services, distribute prospect lists to coaches, maintain the film log system, update recruiting boards in staff room, ensure that all top prospects have film profiles on the network, analyze national trends in recruiting, research new target areas, review each area with individual coaches on a regular basis, maintain combine results, prepare tapes for staff meetings, respond to any position needs on the board, work with coaches on recruiting needs and depth</li><li>Create graphic designs and visuals for recruiting purposes.<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>Daily Operations</strong></div><ul><li>Work with the coaching staff to direct the day to day operations of the sport program. Work with Head Coach and AD to develop short- and long-range planning. Make recommendations to improve/change current policies/procedures. Responsible for developing a manual for recruiting, academics and student-athletes, consistent with university and departmental policy. Responsible for managing and remaining within individual sport budget. Responsible for directing all operations according to university and departmental policy and procedures.</li><li>Maintains Twitter and lnstagram pages for the team.<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>Player/ Parent Contact</strong></div><ul><li>Serve as liaison between coaches and parents - main parent contact<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>Academic Liaison</strong></div><ul><li>Serve as the liaison to the Director of Compliance for admission procedures and assist in filing with the NCAA Eligibility Center for all prospective student-athletes.</li><li>Responsible for compiling and processing academic information on prospects, which includes: preparing pre-application binders for: Admissions, Athletic Director, Head Coach, Recruiting Coordinator, Director of Compliance; this includes: pre-application binders containing the following: pre­ applications for admission, transcripts, test scores, progress reports, high school profile, etc.</li><li>Responsible for maintaining academic paperwork, inform coaches on needed items, maintaining individual files for all players, transcript breakdowns for top prospects or by request of coach</li><li>Assist with the monitoring of academic progress of student-athletes. Establish and maintain an environment conducive to the welfare and academic success of the student-athlete. Establish and maintain effective interactions with students, staff, and administrators.</li><li>Adheres to all policy and procedures, including prohibition of contacting faculty directly.<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>Summer Camps</strong></div><ul><li>Serve as director for all summer camps, team camps, and clinics.</li><li>Follow all departmental and NCAA guidelines related to summer camps and clinics.</li><li>Work with staff in order to develop the logistics of each camps.</li><li>Maintain proper records of each camps, individual campers/teams, and all financial transactions.</li><li>Provide full disclosure of each camp to business office.</li><li>Responsible for all recruiting aspects of summer camps. This includes: providing lists of prospects attending camp to coaches, separating prospects from general campers on day of camp, providing recorded times to coaches during camp<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>Special Events</strong></div><ul><li>Coordinate and organize the end of year banquet and senior send off for each season. Schedule and oversee all logistics of event</li><li>Assist senior department staff with special events related to basketball (i.e. Hoopalooza, Hall of Fame, Golf Tournaments, Reunions, etc.)<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>Liaison for Compliance</strong></div><ul><li>Maintain complete and thorough knowledge of all NCAA rules, both adopted and submitted for consideration at NCAA</li><li>Educate coaches on all rules, serving as liaison to Director of Compliance.</li><li>Adhere to the \"Ask before you Act\" philosophy on all compliance matters.</li><li>Maintain effective records and correspondence related to all compliance related matters.</li><li>Maintaining and turn in phone logs to compliance</li><li>Maintain and submit all CARA reports, time management reports and any additional compliance reports required for the program.</li><li>Complete all required paperwork as required by the NCAA Compliance Office.</li><li>Prepare reports, records, and other related documents; prepare request for national letter of intent and applications, monitor grant-in-aid list and numbers, with a sensitivity to counters<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>Team Travel</strong></div><ul><li>Direct and coordinate team travel for home/away games, post-season championships.</li><li>Set up rooms and meals; logistics of team travel itineraries, rooming lists, practice times.</li><li>Follow all university, departmental and NCAA rules relating to team travel.</li><li>Manage team travel within available budgeted resources, receiving preapproval for all transactions.</li><li>Manage complimentary ticket list according to NCAA rules and allotment of tickets per contract.</li><li>Submit for payment all invoices, submitting travel requests and vouchers in a timely fashion.<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>Community Relations</strong></div><ul><li>Coordinate and plan visits annually to schools, hospitals and volunteer opportunities in the community for student-athletes.</li><li>Initiate and secure opportunities annually for coaching staff to speak to local groups, advisory boards, philanthropic organizations, elementary schools, etc.</li><li>Responsible for communicating, promoting program via social media.<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>Scheduling</strong></div><ul><li>Responsible for scheduling contests to develop team competition schedules that meets revenue obligations, maintains competitive balance, fits within team travel budgetary resources, is viewed by fans as attractive, remains within NCAA parameters, and positions team strategically for post-season competition (i.e. seeding)</li><li>Maintain relationships with regional rivals to continue home/home series (SIU, MTSU, etc.).</li><li>Request preparation of game contracts to AD office. Submit contracts for away games to AD office for signature and processing.</li><li>Strategically research data pertaining to game guarantees to maximize revenue opportunities (WinAD).</li><li>Meet all scheduling requirements, if any, as stipulated by conference membership.<br><br></li></ul><div>As a member of the Murray State University Athletic Department, you shall comply with all applicable NCAA rules and regulations as provided in the NCAA Division I Manual. If you are found in violation of NCAA regulations, you shall be subject to disciplinary or corrective action as set forth in the provisions of the NCAA enforcement procedures, including suspension without pay or termination of employment for significant repetitive violations.</div> Men's Basketball https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12808 2026-08-04T09:28:24-05:00 2026-08-04T09:28:25-05:00 Assistant Professor, Physiology <div>The primary teaching responsibilities will be upper level Animal Physiology, which is taken by Pre-Medical, Pre-Dental, and Pre-Optometry majors who are close to applying for professional school. The candidate will also teach Human Physiology, as well as some introductory biology courses. There will be opportunities to teach other upper level courses and graduate level courses in the successful applicant's area of expertise. The research area within physiology is open, but preference will be given to candidates with expertise in animal physiology at the cellular or systems level. The successful candidate will conduct research and publish their work, pursue external funding, mentor undergraduate and graduate student research, and advise students pursuing professional degrees in health-related fields.</div> Biological Sciences https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12738 2026-07-15T15:52:57-05:00 2026-07-15T15:52:57-05:00 Veterinary Diagnostician/Assistant Professor <div>Serves as liaison between the laboratory and customers, receiving diagnostic samples, routing for testing, serving as a case coordinator, releasing test results, and answering customer and staff questions.<br><br></div><ul><li>Liaison with referring veterinarians, owners, staff, food producers, government agencies, and other laboratories.</li><li>Receives diagnostic samples for testing (e.g., takes case history, unloads animals, preparing and routing laboratory samples, etc.)</li><li>Review and coordinate laboratory cases; release diagnostic laboratory reports and ensure accuracy, clarity and completeness.</li><li>Supervises shipping and receiving personnel. Ensures Receiving Area is manned during all business hours (including lunch).</li><li>Monitors current processes and policies for receiving and routing incoming cases; ensures regulatory compliance to include accreditation standards, develops new procedures and policies as needed.</li><li>Participates in and ensures compliance with the quality management, biosafety, and bio­security programs.</li><li>Serve as the coordinator for disease notifications, including those involving select agents, to the appropriate authorities.</li><li>Develops Continuing Education Programs for Veterinarians; find speakers, professional instructors and sponsors for programs; invites veterinarians, organizes program</li><li>Develops educational programs for presentation to primary and secondary students; may be veterinary or animal science in nature; distributes or presents to area schools.</li><li>Provides tours and educational programs for post-secondary education groups, stakeholder groups at BVC.</li><li>Attends and represents BVC at stakeholder meetings, veterinary meetings; provides outreach to veterinarians, farmers and pet owners as determined by the Director.</li><li>Perform special projects as determined by the Director.</li></ul> Breathitt Veterinary Center https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12845 2026-08-28T10:58:32-05:00 2026-08-28T10:58:33-05:00 Dental Hygiene Administrative Specialist <div>The Dental Hygiene Administrative Specialist for the Dental Hygiene Program provides comprehensive administrative, financial, and operational support for the Dental Hygiene Program and patient clinic. This position is responsible for coordinating daily clinic operations, managing patient scheduling and records, supervising front office activities, maintaining clinic inventories, processing financial transactions, supporting faculty and students, ensuring compliance and regulatory requirements, and providing exceptional customer service to patients. The Dental Hygiene Administrative Specialist serves as the primary point of contact for patients, students, faculty, and external healthcare providers, ensuring the efficient and effective operation of the teaching clinic and program.<br><br></div><ul><li>Coordinate all front office operations for the Dental Hygiene Clinic</li><li>Create and maintain confidential patient and student records in accordance with university and regulatory requirements.</li><li>Obtain dental radiographs, medial clearances, referrals, and other documentation from healthcare providers.</li><li>Maintain patient recall systems and generate recall lists for student scheduling.</li><li>Develop and maintain a patient classification system to ensure equitable patient distribution among students.</li><li>Assist students in identifying, recruiting, and scheduling patients needed to meet clinical competencies.</li><li>Supervise and train student workers assigned to reception during clinic sessions.</li><li>Maintain financial records, balance daily clinic financial transactions, reconcile purchasing card transactions, invoices, and vendor charges.</li><li>Manage inventory of office supplies, educational and patient care supplies, and dental, clinical, laboratory supplies.</li><li>Process requisitions and special purchase requests for faculty and instructors.</li><li>Arrange delivery of medical gases, including nitrous oxide and oxygen.</li><li>Process dosimetry services for faculty, staff, and students.</li><li>Ensure clinic documentation complies with applicable university, state, and federal regulations.</li><li>Manage retention and destruction of patient records in accordance with record retention policies.</li><li>Maintain confidentiality of patient health information in compliance with HIPAA requirements.</li><li>Enter clinic schedules and student assignments into the dental clinic management software</li><li>Create and maintain user accounts and passwords within the clinic software system.</li><li>Maintain active and inactive patient records.</li><li>Proctor examinations as requested by faculty.</li><li>Support program outreach and recruitment activities.</li><li>Other duties as assigned.</li></ul> Dental Hygiene https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12833 2026-08-19T16:08:58-05:00 2026-08-19T16:09:00-05:00 Director of Expo Center <div>The Expo Director is responsible for the successful operation of the Cherry West Kentucky Livestock and Exposition (Expo) Center, a 2,748 seat multi-event building.<br><br></div><ul><li>Serve as the primary liaison between building users and University staff.</li><li>Prepare and direct the preparation of marketing/promotional campaigns designed to enhance the facilities’ reputation and maximize usage, as well as making presentations to organizations and groups concerning the capabilities and capacities of the Expo.</li><li>Establish contractual agreements, overall budgets, operating policies and procedures, as well as identifying operating needs; improve logistics processes and requirements of the facilities.</li><li>Perform operating and financial analyses to ensure proficiency and optimum realization from assets expended.</li><li>Meet material/equipment/animal handling requirements, standards for safety for MSU regulations, Fire Marshall Codes, and OSHA.</li><li>Proactively seek customer satisfaction perceptions and modify goals accordingly.</li><li>Administer appropriate forms for all inventories, equipment, food accountability, and monitor building and ancillary components.</li><li>Supervision of the Expo work force of full-time and student employees and training of the Expo work force.</li><li>Must support and promote the missions of the Huston School of Agriculture and related events and must maintain current promoters/proactively seek new events and have vision to promote Expo to the next level.</li><li>Oversee the Farm Equipment Training Program in the Hutson School of Agriculture.</li><li>Directs the supervision of specialists assigned to the various disciplines offered at Expo Center and evaluates the results of specialized programs.</li><li>Coordinates with the supervisor on appropriate strategies to foster events engaging community aligned with the educational goals supporting the mission of Murray State University.</li><li>Other duties as assigned.</li></ul> West KY Expo Ctr https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12763 2026-07-21T13:00:02-05:00 2026-07-21T13:00:03-05:00 Assistant Professor, Organic Chemistry <div>The Department of Chemistry invites applications from individuals committed to being excellent teacher-scholars at a primarily undergraduate institution. The successful candidate will be expected to teach a 3/2 course load including foundational organic chemistry courses, teaching laboratory courses, and advanced courses in their sub-discipline to both undergraduate and graduate (Masters) students. Candidates with expertise in materials science and/or polymer chemistry are especially encouraged to apply. The faculty candidate will be expected to establish a viable research program, supported by external funding, and supervise/train student researchers at both the undergraduate and graduate (Masters) levels. The faculty candidate will also be expected to participate in service activities at the department, collegiate, and university level as needed. The candidate hired for this position will be assigned laboratory and office space appropriate to their teaching and research needs.</div> Chemistry https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12683 2026-06-23T15:22:26-05:00 2026-06-23T15:22:27-05:00 Assistant Professor, Counseling <div>The successful candidate will (1) teach a minimum of three courses per semester; (2) coordinate counseling operations for the Counseling and Assessment Center, as needed; (3) maintain an advising caseload of graduate and undergraduate students; (4) supervise practicum and internship students; (5) engage in professional research and scholarly activities; (6) pursue involvement in appropriate professional organizations at the national, regional, and/or state levels; and (7) be actively involved in departmental, college, and university committees.</div> Ed Studies Ldrshp Cnslng https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12854 2026-09-03T12:46:02-05:00 2026-09-03T12:46:03-05:00 Administrative Assistant I <div>General office duties.<br><br></div><ul><li>First point of contact for office visitors; answer phone and draft messages, write and distribute emails, correspondence memos, letters, faxes, and forms.</li><li>Assist in managing all budget activities including accounting.</li><li>Organize and maintain electronic and paper files of grant documents, accounting documents and resources.</li><li>Assist with website updates, social media, and office calendar.</li><li>Mange office supply inventory and ordering as well as outside vendor requests.</li><li>Manage scheduling of meeting rooms, food ordering, pickup/delivery for meetings and events.</li><li>Assist with travel arrangements for staff.</li><li>Assist Director and staff with quarterly and annual reports as well as other tasks.</li><li>Develop a working relationship with our host as well as our program offices of UofL and UK schools of medicine.</li><li>Be able to travel in our 12-county region as well as statewide meetings and conferences.</li></ul> Purchase Area Health Edu Center (Grant) https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12835 2026-08-21T08:56:59-05:00 2026-08-21T08:56:59-05:00 Systems Administrator <div>Reporting to the Director of Systems Administration, the Systems Administrator assists the team in maintaining, upgrading and securing multiple data centers between on-prem and cloud services, to support enterprise computing, storage, data integrity and backup infrastructure and services.<br><br></div><ul><li>Deploy, support and maintain Windows, Linux and Unix virtual and physical environments.</li><li>Patch and maintain the enterprise virtualization infrastructure. Monitor cluster resource utilization to ensure high availability and performance. Coordinate with networking administrators to configure virtual networking and VLAN assignments.</li><li>Active Directory (AD/Entra), Group Policies (GPOs), LAPS and core domain server upgrades and patching. Implement, coordinate and communicate AD hygiene best practices.</li><li>Execute the patching lifestyle for all servers and core infrastructure for vulnerability mitigation.</li><li>Monitor and manage enterprise storage arrays (SAN/NAS). Oversee the daily backup and replication schedules, verify backup integrity, and participate in regular Disaster Recovery exercises.</li><li>Administer, setup and maintain network file shares across NFS and CIFS environments. Troubleshoot access issues, manage quotas, and ensure data classification compliance.</li><li>Utilize and maintain enterprise monitoring tools to track system performance, incidents and communicate to system stakeholders for proactive mitigation. Install endpoint monitoring and detection agents and maintain detection rules for servers. Assist and respond to system incidents.</li><li>Maintain the back-end VDI infrastructure through patching and upgrades.</li><li>Act as a liaison between vendors, technical personnel and end users, utilizing internal ticketing and vendor support sites as necessary. Provide technical support to vendors and end users as appropriate.</li><li>Assist in installation and care of physical hardware within data centers. Rack and relocate servers and blades.</li><li>Understanding of SSL/TLS certificate request and installation to secure endpoints. Monitor certificate expiration timelines.</li><li>Demonstrable knowledge of scripting and automation techniques (i.e. Powershell, Bash, Ansible).</li><li>Basic understanding of networking fundamentals, firewalls and secure access principles.</li><li>Demonstrated understanding in system monitoring, auditing, alerting, and troubleshooting practices.</li><li>Develop and maintain technical system documentation and procedures.</li><li>Other duties as assigned.</li></ul> Systems Administration https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12807 2026-08-04T09:26:40-05:00 2026-08-04T09:26:41-05:00 Assistant Professor, Cell Biology <div>The primary teaching responsibilities will be introductory level Cell Biology, upper-level Cell Biology, and an upper-level course in the candidate’s area of expertise. The research area may be in any field of cellular and molecular biology. The successful candidate will conduct research and publish their work, pursue external funding, mentor undergraduate and graduate student research, and advise students pursuing professional degrees in health-related fields.</div> Biological Sciences https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12733 2026-07-15T07:22:56-05:00 2026-07-15T07:22:56-05:00 Instructor/Assistant Professor, Criminal Justice <div>This position will have a teaching load of 12 credit hours per semester. As this is a small undergraduate program, the ability to teach a variety of courses across the criminal justice curriculum is expected. The successful applicant will also be expected to teach graduate level criminal justice courses in the online CRJ concentration of the new MSU MBA program.<br><br><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Teach a variety of courses across the CRJ curriculum suited to experience and expertise.</li><li>Teach graduate level criminal justice courses that make up the online CRJ concentration of the MSU MBA program.</li><li>Serves as academic advisor and professional mentor for students.</li><li>Actively participate in committee work, curriculum and professional development, and service to external stakeholders.</li><li>Liaise with law enforcement agencies in the region.</li><li>Develop in-service training for law enforcement officers.</li><li>Recruit for the Criminal Justice Program as well as the CRJ concentration of the MBA program.</li><li>If ranked as an Assistant Professor, maintain a research agenda.</li><li>Other duties as assigned.</li></ul> Criminal Justice and Social Work"
    },
