    "https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12851": {
      "title": "Murray State University Applicant Portal Site | BVC Business Coordinator",
      "description": "Murray State University Applicant Portal Site | BVC Business Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help BVC Business Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number 20270033NE Job Title BVC Business Coordinator Number of Vacancies 1 About Murray State Located in the West Kentucky region, Murray State University is a public, comprehensive University which offers a low cost of living, low property taxes, and a four-season climate. Murray has a friendly, small-town atmosphere with locally-owned specialty shops and restaurants, an acclaimed community theater, art guild and award-winning public schools. The area is home to Kentucky Lake and Land Between the Lakes, a 170,000-acre National Recreation Area, which offers a wide-range of activities and amenities for residents and visitors alike. Located in close proximity to major cities and nearby access to Interstate 24, Murray is just a few hours from Nashville, St. Louis, Louisville and Memphis. Learn more about Careers at Murray State University. About Murray State Benefits Faculty and staff of Murray State University have access to a comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, retirement, tuition waivers, generous paid holidays, vacation, sick, and paid parental leave, as well as many other benefit offerings. Please refer to the Murray State Benefits page for more information. Equal Opportunity Employment Equal Opportunity Employer/AA. Murray State University does not discriminate based on race, color, national origin, sex, gender, identity, sexual orientation, religion, age, veteran status, disability or political or social viewpoint. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply. Type of Employment Regular Full-Time If Part Time, Enter Hours Per Week Work Location Hopkinsville, KY Employment Term 12 Months Position Type Staff - Non-Exempt (Hourly) Department Breathitt Veterinary Center Summary of Job Duties and Responsibilities Performs administrative support, customer service, research, database management, strategic and budget planning, data analytics, and critical quality control documentation to ensure timely and accurate diagnostic reporting for nationally accredited Level 1 National Animal Health Network laboratory. Initiate diagnostic testing process by creating work process in Laboratory Information Management System. Maintain accurate and detailed customer/vendor account information. Exercise judgement (e.g. determining appropriate vendors, evaluating vendor performance, providing vendor feedback, addressing supply and logistical issues, etc.), to perform administrative functions required to purchase/order/process for payment critical supplies and equipment. Interact with vendor, maintain building security, and ensure visitor compliance with laboratory quality and safety requirements. Assist with grant budget and management Plan/Coordinate internal/external administrative efforts. Create, maintain, and update administrative work processes. Monitor organizational budget and prepare informational reports. Develop budget reports for spending and revenue analysis Interact with vendors and work with procurement to ensure purchasing compliance. Research equipment and supplies for laboratory use Coordinate with other laboratories for administrative and financial processes. Prepare/distribute billing documents and process payments. Review invoices, prepare and approve payments. Reconcile accounting reports with expense and revenues Maintain customer/personnel confidentiality Complete required administrative and financial processes/reports/documents/ deposits etc. Document process deficiencies and participate in developing resolution Special projects as required Liaison with HR and prepare personnel administrative documents Exercise discretion and independent judgment with daily customer interactions to ensure complete and accurate data, fees charged, and fees charged, and customer inquiries. Ensure compliance with critical quality/accreditation standards. Document control for admin work processes (ensure changes are properly documented, approved, implemented, and retained), accurate data input, documenting changes, obtaining appropriate approval for corrections. Creating a paper trail accreditation team to see a start to finish project with all changes properly approved/documented. Complete national accreditation, university, and laboratory required training. In addition to University training, Lab Safety training, Periodic quality training, recognizing hazards, proper reporting of hazards, etc. Review new/changed administrative work processes and document the review was completed. Maintain proficiency, skills, and knowledge to ensure compliance with laboratory quality/capacity requirements necessary to maintain a Level 1 laboratory status. Maintain database knowledge, data entry speed and accuracy, and familiarity with documents submitted to meet Level 1 advertised testing capabilities (e.g. 700-800 tests per day), quality reporting, message automation to nation agencies, and confidentiality. Participate in quality process to include internal audits and national accreditation processes. Verifying data entry accuracy, logging customer complaints and additional customer instructions, creating a clear administrative trail (initial paperwork to final report to billing) for accreditation team members to review during the national visits. Investigate (determine root cause), document, develop corrective actions (how to avoid/minimize incomplete or inaccurate data), and implement corrective actions to eliminate or minimize future issues. Participate in periodic internal audits and non-conformance root cause working groups of work areas (to include other work areas) to ensure compliance with accreditation standards and documentation requirements. Participate in the nation accreditation by answering accreditation team questions (written and verbal), providing documentation showing work processes are followed and they are following internal and external processes. Continually review work area processes used for reliability and proper operation. They must be familiar with submitting problems, participating in developing solutions, and implementing resolution. Must address and clearly document data entry errors (e.g. corrected data, date change made, approval, etc.) and test request changes. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Education Requirements Bachelor’s Degree. Minimum Experience and Skill Requirements Four years office experience in a business, government, or industrial setting. Additional college education and related work experience may be exchanged year for year to meet requirements. Pleasant, proactive personality with the ability to handle demanding situations, quickly adapt to address changing circumstances and personalities, and work as a team Excellent communication, interpersonal, supervisory, multi-tasking, and organizational skills Problem solving ability to troubleshoot deficiencies, identify corrective actions, evaluate new processes and materials/equipment, implement plans, and develop preventive actions Alertness, initiative, memory for verbal and written directions and details, analytical ability. Ability to plan and make decisions often without instruction or supervision Proficient computer skills, internet research, and the use of Microsoft Word, Microsoft Excel, and email. Preferred Education and/or Experience Qualifications Prefer facility maintenance certification, or trade license (e.g., electrical, plumbing, heating and cooling etc.). Familiar/experience with Building automation systems preferred Posting Date 09/03/2026 Closing Date 09/17/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Hourly Rate/Annual Salary $16.75 (Additional pay dependent upon qualifications) Staff Grade 105 Work Hours May be required to respond on weekends, holidays and after hours for building functions and meetings. Physical Demands Will handle blood, tissue, and other samples submitted for diagnostic work. Additionally, there are pungent odors associated with laboratory work Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you currently have a Bachelor's degree? Yes No * How many years of office experience do you have? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document 412 Sparks Hall Murray, KY 42071 - msu.hr@murraystate.edu - (270) 809-2146 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
