    "https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12845": {
      "title": "Murray State University Applicant Portal Site | Dental Hygiene Administrative Specialist",
      "description": "Murray State University Applicant Portal Site | Dental Hygiene Administrative Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Dental Hygiene Administrative Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number 20270029NE Job Title Dental Hygiene Administrative Specialist Number of Vacancies 1 About Murray State Located in the West Kentucky region, Murray State University is a public, comprehensive University which offers a low cost of living, low property taxes, and a four-season climate. Murray has a friendly, small-town atmosphere with locally-owned specialty shops and restaurants, an acclaimed community theater, art guild and award-winning public schools. The area is home to Kentucky Lake and Land Between the Lakes, a 170,000-acre National Recreation Area, which offers a wide-range of activities and amenities for residents and visitors alike. Located in close proximity to major cities and nearby access to Interstate 24, Murray is just a few hours from Nashville, St. Louis, Louisville and Memphis. Learn more about Careers at Murray State University. About Murray State Benefits Faculty and staff of Murray State University have access to a comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, retirement, tuition waivers, generous paid holidays, vacation, sick, and paid parental leave, as well as many other benefit offerings. Please refer to the Murray State Benefits page for more information. Equal Opportunity Employment Equal Opportunity Employer/AA. Murray State University does not discriminate based on race, color, national origin, sex, gender, identity, sexual orientation, religion, age, veteran status, disability or political or social viewpoint. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply. Type of Employment Regular Full-Time If Part Time, Enter Hours Per Week Work Location Murray, KY Employment Term 12 Months Position Type Staff - Non-Exempt (Hourly) Department Dental Hygiene Summary of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Dental Hygiene Administrative Specialist for the Dental Hygiene Program provides comprehensive administrative, financial, and operational support for the Dental Hygiene Program and patient clinic. This position is responsible for coordinating daily clinic operations, managing patient scheduling and records, supervising front office activities, maintaining clinic inventories, processing financial transactions, supporting faculty and students, ensuring compliance and regulatory requirements, and providing exceptional customer service to patients. The Dental Hygiene Administrative Specialist serves as the primary point of contact for patients, students, faculty, and external healthcare providers, ensuring the efficient and effective operation of the teaching clinic and program. Coordinate all front office operations for the Dental Hygiene Clinic Create and maintain confidential patient and student records in accordance with university and regulatory requirements. Obtain dental radiographs, medial clearances, referrals, and other documentation from healthcare providers. Maintain patient recall systems and generate recall lists for student scheduling. Develop and maintain a patient classification system to ensure equitable patient distribution among students. Assist students in identifying, recruiting, and scheduling patients needed to meet clinical competencies. Supervise and train student workers assigned to reception during clinic sessions. Maintain financial records, balance daily clinic financial transactions, reconcile purchasing card transactions, invoices, and vendor charges. Manage inventory of office supplies, educational and patient care supplies, and dental, clinical, laboratory supplies. Process requisitions and special purchase requests for faculty and instructors. Arrange delivery of medical gases, including nitrous oxide and oxygen. Process dosimetry services for faculty, staff, and students. Ensure clinic documentation complies with applicable university, state, and federal regulations. Manage retention and destruction of patient records in accordance with record retention policies. Maintain confidentiality of patient health information in compliance with HIPAA requirements. Enter clinic schedules and student assignments into the dental clinic management software Create and maintain user accounts and passwords within the clinic software system. Maintain active and inactive patient records. Proctor examinations as requested by faculty. Support program outreach and recruitment activities. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Education Requirements Two years of college. Minimum Experience and Skill Requirements Four years of upper-level office experience in a business, government, or industrial setting. Additional college and related experience may be exchanged year-for-year to meet qualifications. Alertness, initiative, attention to accuracy, memory for oral and written directions or details, ability to plan and make decisions often without instruction or supervision. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Keyboarding, filing, MS Office Suite programs, office procedures; bookkeeping may be required. Excellent decision-making skills, problem solving and organizational skills. Pleasant disposition and demeanor. Ability to multitask. Preferred Education and/or Experience Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree in business, healthcare administration, office administration highly preferred. Posting Date 08/28/2026 Closing Date 09/11/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Hourly Rate/Annual Salary $15.95 (Additional pay dependent upon qualifications) Staff Grade 104 Work Hours Normal working hours. Physical Demands Normal for office environment. Occasional lifting of supplies and equipment. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a minimum of two years of college credit? Yes No * How many years of upper-level administrative experience do you have? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document 412 Sparks Hall Murray, KY 42071 - msu.hr@murraystate.edu - (270) 809-2146 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
