    "https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12835": {
      "title": "Murray State University Applicant Portal Site",
      "description": "Murray State University Applicant Portal Site | Systems Administrator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Systems Administrator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Along with the application, the following items must be included: Letter of application Resume For best consideration, please submit a completed application along​ with all required materials​ by September 4, 2026.​ Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Job Details Position Information Posting Number 20260048EX Job Title Systems Administrator Number of Vacancies 1 About Murray State Located in the West Kentucky region, Murray State University is a public, comprehensive University which offers a low cost of living, low property taxes, and a four-season climate. Murray has a friendly, small-town atmosphere with locally-owned specialty shops and restaurants, an acclaimed community theater, art guild and award-winning public schools. The area is home to Kentucky Lake and Land Between the Lakes, a 170,000-acre National Recreation Area, which offers a wide-range of activities and amenities for residents and visitors alike. Located in close proximity to major cities and nearby access to Interstate 24, Murray is just a few hours from Nashville, St. Louis, Louisville and Memphis. Learn more about Careers at Murray State University. About Murray State Benefits Faculty and staff of Murray State University have access to a comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, retirement, tuition waivers, generous paid holidays, vacation, sick, and paid parental leave, as well as many other benefit offerings. Please refer to the Murray State Benefits page for more information. Equal Opportunity Employment Equal Opportunity Employer/AA. Murray State University does not discriminate based on race, color, national origin, sex, gender, identity, sexual orientation, religion, age, veteran status, disability or political or social viewpoint. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply. Type of Employment Regular Full-Time If Part Time, Enter Hours Per Week Work Location Murray, KY Employment Term 12 Months Position Type Staff - Exempt (Monthly) Department Systems Administration Summary of Job Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Director of Systems Administration, the Systems Administrator assists the team in maintaining, upgrading and securing multiple data centers between on-prem and cloud services, to support enterprise computing, storage, data integrity and backup infrastructure and services. Deploy, support and maintain Windows, Linux and Unix virtual and physical environments. Patch and maintain the enterprise virtualization infrastructure. Monitor cluster resource utilization to ensure high availability and performance. Coordinate with networking administrators to configure virtual networking and VLAN assignments. Active Directory (AD/Entra), Group Policies (GPOs), LAPS and core domain server upgrades and patching. Implement, coordinate and communicate AD hygiene best practices. Execute the patching lifestyle for all servers and core infrastructure for vulnerability mitigation. Monitor and manage enterprise storage arrays ( SAN / NAS ). Oversee the daily backup and replication schedules, verify backup integrity, and participate in regular Disaster Recovery exercises. Administer, setup and maintain network file shares across NFS and CIFS environments. Troubleshoot access issues, manage quotas, and ensure data classification compliance. Utilize and maintain enterprise monitoring tools to track system performance, incidents and communicate to system stakeholders for proactive mitigation. Install endpoint monitoring and detection agents and maintain detection rules for servers. Assist and respond to system incidents. Maintain the back-end VDI infrastructure through patching and upgrades. Act as a liaison between vendors, technical personnel and end users, utilizing internal ticketing and vendor support sites as necessary. Provide technical support to vendors and end users as appropriate. Assist in installation and care of physical hardware within data centers. Rack and relocate servers and blades. Understanding of SSL / TLS certificate request and installation to secure endpoints. Monitor certificate expiration timelines. Demonstrable knowledge of scripting and automation techniques (i.e. Powershell, Bash, Ansible). Basic understanding of networking fundamentals, firewalls and secure access principles. Demonstrated understanding in system monitoring, auditing, alerting, and troubleshooting practices. Develop and maintain technical system documentation and procedures. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Education Requirements Bachelor’s Degree required. Minimum Experience and Skill Requirements One year of experience as a Windows and/or Linux Systems administrator within a virtual environment is required. Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Ability to learn new technologies and adapt to change. Excellent troubleshooting, communication, documentation, and organizational skills. Preferred Education and/or Experience Qualifications Degree in computer-related field preferred. Physical Demands Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. Work Hours Normal business hours. Will be required to participate in an on-call rotation and schedule maintenance windows outside of normal business hours as needed. Hourly Rate/Annual Salary $50,878 (grade minimum) -$66,560 (grade midpoint). Final salary will be dependent upon applicant's qualifications. Staff Grade 114 Posting Details Posting Date 08/21/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Along with the application, the following items must be included: Letter of application Resume For best consideration, please submit a completed application along​ with all required materials​ by September 4, 2026.​ Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you currently have a Bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you have one year of experience as a Windows and/or Linux Systems Administrator within a virtual environment? Yes No * This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship.  Are you a US citizen or permanent resident? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document 412 Sparks Hall Murray, KY 42071 - msu.hr@murraystate.edu - (270) 809-2146 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
